<title>SWEDEN: FORECAST-Sandvik '96 profit 17 pct down.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Sandvik '96 profit 17 pct down.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish engineer Sandvik was expected to post a profit after financial items of 4.65 billion crowns for 1996, according to a Reuters poll of 13 analysts on Thursday.</p>
<p>This compared to a profit of 5.62 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>Forecasts for 1996 varied between 4.45 billion crowns to 4.83 billion crowns.</p>
<p>Analysts on average forecast a profit after financial items of 5.06 billion crowns in 1998.</p>
<p>They forecast a dividend for 1996 of six crowns a share.</p>
<p>Analysts interviewed for the poll were from Aros, Carnegie, Deutsche Morgan Grenfell, Enskilda, Fiba Nordic, Fischer Partners, Goldman Sachs, Handelsbanken, James Capel, Kleinwort Benson, Matteus, Morgan Stanley, and Swedbank.</p>
<p>Sandvik will release its annual report on February 24.</p>
<p>    (Mln skr)	     AVG	RANGE     ANALYSTS</p>
<p> Profit after fin '96   4,651   4,449-4,830    13</p>
<p> Profit after fin '97   5,057   4,180-5,791    13</p>
<p> Profit after fin '98   5,777   4,940-6,592    11</p>
<p> Dividend '96 (SKR)	6.10    5.50-6.50     11</p>
<p>-- Jorgen Osterberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1008</p>
